==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Half-Off: S. Rare}}

==Battleground==
*5 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*15 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Puffzerker]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Wicked Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
**1 [[Red EnerG]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**1 [[Puffzerker]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Super Rare Cats are half-off for this Otherworld Colosseum, and every single one you send creates an identical clone on the field after two seconds—it's a buy one, get one free! This gimmick is particularly easy to take advantage of with Extra Money cats like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], where you can start stacking unfathomable amounts of support to completely obliterate most stages.

Round 1 is easy; stall out Puffzerker using Bullet Train Cat and build up your wallet over time, then go in on the offensive with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cats]], and Can Can Cats once he dies. The Capies can be walled off using [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], since it's effectively like spamming 4 meatshields. There is zero concern for cash here, so you can just start spamming everything off-cooldown to quickly overwhelm the enemies. Bring a Shield Piercer to help clean up Wicked Face, if you want, that is.

